# GitHub workflow

## Push authentication

Integrated terminal (VS Code / Cursor): pushes work via injected askpass — `GIT_ASKPASS` + `VSCODE_GIT_IPC_HANDLE` route credentials to the editor's GitHub session. No stored token, `gh`, or `credential.helper` required.

**Do not** conclude "can't push / no credentials" just because `git config credential.helper`, `~/.git-credentials`, and `gh` are absent — check `echo $GIT_ASKPASS` first.

**Cursor agent shells** do not get those env vars injected. Agent `git push` may fail unless the user runs `gh auth setup-git` or pushes via Source Control UI.

## Branch workflow

- `a-haz/aimanhazim.com` and `a-haz/pyroscout` deploy from `main`; direct commits to `main` are normal.
- `.github/workflows/sitemap.yml` auto-commits `sitemap.xml` on HTML changes — don't hand-edit it; `git pull --rebase origin main` before the next push.
- `a-haz/project-00` was renamed to `a-haz/pyroscout`.
- Direct pushes to `main` are classifier-gated — commit locally, ask before pushing unless the user says "push".

## Commit authorship

Git identity: `aiman-hazim <dev@aimanhazim.com>`.

**Commit as the user only** — never append `Co-Authored-By` trailers (Cursor, Claude, etc.).

**Agents:** use `./scripts/commit.sh` (not bare `git commit`). It activates `.githooks/`, which strips any injected trailers. After clone, run `./scripts/setup-git-hooks.sh` once so hooks apply to all commits in that clone.

Do not rewrite history to strip old trailers unless asked.
